tty: hold a wide-gamut output to sRGB in the display engine

An output with `srgb-gamut` set has sRGB's colours mapped onto its own
primaries, read from its EDID, so a wide-gamut panel stops stretching
every colour to its own and matches an sRGB monitor beside it. The
CRTC's DEGAMMA_LUT decodes sRGB to linear light, its CTM takes sRGB's
primaries to the panel's at the panel's white, and GAMMA_LUT encodes
sRGB again, with a gamma-control client's ramp composed after it. All
three go in one atomic commit, so it costs nothing to draw. An output
whose primaries are sRGB's already, or whose EDID gives none, is left
as it is.

A gamma-control client's step, such as a night light's glide, changes the
ramp alone, so it sets GAMMA_LUT alone: the degamma curve and the matrix
are set again only when the matrix changes.

