 ```
 
+### `srgb-gamut`
+
+Show colours on this output as sRGB, rather than stretched to its own primaries.
+
+niri draws in sRGB and sends it to the output as it is.
+On a screen whose primaries reach past sRGB's, such as many OLED laptop panels, every colour then comes out oversaturated.
+With `srgb-gamut`, niri reads the primaries the screen's EDID declares and has the display engine map sRGB to them, through the CRTC's degamma curve, colour matrix and gamma curve, at no cost to rendering.
+White and greys stay as they were.
+
+It needs the driver to offer `DEGAMMA_LUT`, `CTM` and `GAMMA_LUT`, and an EDID that declares primaries; niri logs a warning when either is missing.
+A gamma control client, such as a night light, still applies on top.
+
+```kdl
+output "eDP-1" {
+    srgb-gamut
+}
+```
+
 ### `focus-at-startup`
 
